lowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T00:11:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T00:11:11Z","body":"@Changryy Can you look into [rebasing this PR](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#updating-your-branch) to fix merge conflicts?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3937726641/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4006336837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108563#issuecomment-4006336837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108563","id":4006336837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uy9lF","user":{"login":"Changryy","id":35406747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NDA2NzQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35406747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy","html_url":"https://github.com/Changryy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T16:36:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T16:36:31Z","body":"> I think we need to have a better parsing solution so all of this checking doesn't have to be done manually just for determining if it should add a closing bracket.\r\n\r\nIt could be changed to work with the `delimiter_cache`, but then the way delimiters are cached also has to change in order to track standalone delimiters. Alternatively we could make a separate cache just for standalone delimiters. Caching the delimiters would also allow this to work across several lines. As with any cache it does however come with the risk of the cache becoming outdated or inaccurate in other ways, which would break the functionality and cause bugs that are difficult to track down\r\n\r\nPersonally I would suggest using this system for now, creating unit tests for all the edge cases, and replacing the system later down the line when a cache-based alternative has been made that passes the tests. Its a very self contained system so it can easily be replaced later without breaking anything","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4006336837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]